  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Continued support for operations of Sahara Forest project in Jordan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SFP will continue to develop the project towards scale up, and also conduct activities that have their own impact both locally and globally. 
Continued operations: Demonstrate and showcase modern climate smart agriculture in Jordan. 
She Grows Training Program: Training of additional 170 women in climate smart agriculture in partnership with HTU. 
Work to diversify funding: 
Commercial Development: Continuously improve the Sahara Forest Project business plan for Jordan with local partners and local due diligence. Obtain land area and saltwater pipeline. Further enhance existing collaborations with commercial partners such as Bama, and attract investors and international donors. Goal is to have strong commitment end of Q2. 
Green the Desert Platform: Testing and trials of carbon storage in biomass as a carbon negative climate solution to be replicated in Jordan and the wider region in line with the IPCC report in partnership with Bellona.</narrative>
  </description>
